+Vinegar, particularly apple cider vinegar, supports glucose regulation and can be used in bean soaking to optimize pH for phytase enzyme activity. Its characteristic acid is [acetic acid](/docs/substances/bioactive-compounds/acetic-acid). The USDA panel on this page does not report a measured acetic acid quantity [3]. The studied comparison, vinegar with a starchy meal, is recorded on [BRS6-FM1-PM1 Glucose Appearance Kinetics](/docs/biological-targets/brs6/fm1/brs6-fm1-pm1-glucose-appearance-kinetics#pm1-f6).
 
